    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Davis R users,<div>I have a question posted on SO about improving the resolution of a PDF downloaded from a Shiny app. I am using dygraphs, so need to convert the html dygraphs object to a PDF. This works, but my plotted points on the PDF are fuzzy.</div><div><br></div><div>Here is the question with a minimal example. I haven&#39;t had any response on SO thus far, so I thought someone in this group may be able to help.</div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/questions/40795357/improve-resolution-of-dygraphs-plotted-points-in-pdf-created-in-shiny-app\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stackoverflow.com/questions/40795357/improve-resolution-of-dygraphs-plotted-points-in-pdf-created-in-shiny-app&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467116116000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3KYoNIgSlyYaQs3XGUDdVS\">http://stackoverflow.com/questions/40795357/improve-resolution-of-dygraphs-plotted-points-in-pdf-created-in-shiny-app</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>Thank you,</div><div>Katie<br clear=\"all\"><div><br></div>-- <br><div class=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><font size=\"1\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\" color=\"#666666\">--</font><div><font style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\" color=\"#666666\" size=\"2\">Katherine Ransom</font><div><font style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\" color=\"#666666\" size=\"2\">PhD Candidate</font></div><div><font style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\" color=\"#666666\" size=\"2\">Hydrologic Sciences Graduate Group</font></div></div><div><font style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\" color=\"#666666\" size=\"2\">UC Davis</font></div><div><br></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>\r\n</div></div>\r\n"
    ]
